{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EZK",
  "chapter": 13,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel that prophesy, and say thou to them that prophesy out of their own hearts, Hear ye the word of the LORD;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the foolish prophets, that follow their own spirit, and have seen nothing!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Israel, thy prophets are like the foxes in the deserts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye have not gone up into the gaps, neither made up the hedge for the house of Israel to stand in the battle in the day of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have seen vanity and lying divination, saying, The LORD saith: and the LORD hath not sent them: and they have made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "others",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to hope that they would confirm the word.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have ye not seen a vain vision, and have ye not spoken a lying divination, whereas ye say, The LORD saith ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", although I have not spoken?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye have spoken vanity, and seen lies, therefore, behold, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against you, saith the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my hand shall be upon the prophets that see vanity, and that divine lies: they shall not be in the assembly of my people, neither shall they be written in the writing of the house of Israel, neither shall they enter into the land of Israel; and ye shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because, even because they have seduced my people, saying, Peace; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no peace; and one built up a wall, and lo, others daubed it with untempered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mortar",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say to them who daub ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with untempered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mortar",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that it shall fall: there shall be an overflowing shower; and ye, O great hailstones, shall fall; and a stormy wind shall rend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, when the wall hath fallen, shall it not be said to you, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the daubing with which ye have daubed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even rend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with a stormy wind in my fury; and there shall be an overflowing shower in my anger, and great hailstones in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fury to consume ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So will I break down the wall that ye have daubed with untempered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mortar",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and bring it down to the ground, so that its foundation shall be made bare, and it shall fall, and ye shall be consumed in the midst of it: and ye shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus will I accomplish my wrath upon the wall, and upon them that have daubed it with untempered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mortar",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and will say to you, The wall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", neither they that daubed it;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To wit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the prophets of Israel who prophesy concerning Jerusalem, and who see visions of peace for her, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no peace, saith the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise, thou son of man, set thy face against the daughters of thy people, who prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy thou against them,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "women",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that sew pillows to all arm-holes, and make kerchiefs upon the head of every stature to hunt souls! Will ye hunt the souls of my people, and will ye save the souls alive ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And will ye profane me among my people for handfuls of barley and for pieces of bread, to slay the souls that should not die, and to save the souls alive that should not live, by your lying to my people that hear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lies?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against your pillows, with which ye there hunt the souls to make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fly, and I will tear them from your arms, and will let the souls go, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the souls that ye hunt to make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your kerchiefs also will I tear, and deliver my people out of your hand, and they shall no more be in your hand to be hunted; and ye shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because with lies ye have made the heart of the righteous sad, whom I have not made sad; and strengthened the hands of the wicked, that he should not return from his wicked way, by promising him life:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.13.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.13.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ye shall see no more vanity, nor divine divinations: for I will deliver my people out of your hand: and ye shall know that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
